    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a favorable setup against Triston Rogers, benefiting from a +16% park adjustment and solid momentum, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a high-leverage matchup against Lucas Giolito, whose 5.37 xERA provides a clear path to production. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also projects as an elite play, drawing a prime lead-off spot against Michael Melton; his projected xwOBA of 0.386 makes him our most efficient bet for run scoring and potential stolen base opportunities, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe are forced to navigate significant difficulty against Zack Wheeler, which drags down the outlook for **Andy Pages** (48.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (55.23). While **Kyle Tucker** remains a start due to his inherent floor, the elite arm of Wheeler and his tendency to suppress stolen bases make both outfielders high-risk pivots. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (46.33), who fell just shy of the threshold. Despite his strong platoon advantage against the lefty Macko, the high-skill ceiling of Macko\u2019s pitching metrics favored the defensive consistency of our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Liam Hicks** and **Andy Pages** as lineups remain pending; should **Liam Hicks** be dropped from the order, we will shift focus to reserve depth to ensure our daily game caps are managed with maximum efficiency.",
